Fuel Divergence Atlas — verification gate, signed by the author.

WHAT THIS SIGNATURE COVERS

Judgement, not arithmetic. The mechanical claims are established by checks in
qa/ and can be re-run by anyone; a reader should verify them there rather than
take this signature's word for them:

  qa/09_reproduce.json      clean-clone rebuild, 251 keys diffed against the
                            committed stats.json, verdict REPRODUCED
  qa/10_eia_crosscheck.json published shares vs values read from EIA's own CSV,
                            verdict AGREES, worst share difference 0.000000
  provenance_hashes_match   SHA-256 of every raw input vs logs/provenance.jsonl
  16 integrity checks       all passing, reported in stats.json

WHAT THE AUTHOR ATTESTS

The author has read the limitations and the judgement calls recorded in this
package and accepts them. The certification-fuel and EN 15940 values carried
over from FUELDIV are the ones they confirmed against their sources under that
project's signed gate. They have read the results of the reproduction,
provenance and EIA cross-checks. They accept the breakdown-point treatment of
FAME density, including that 18 early-year rows do depend on the EN 14214 figure
and are reported as doing so. No number in this package is described as
measured, and no direction is asserted that the specifications do not establish.

THE FOUR JUDGEMENT CALLS, AND THE AUTHOR'S RULING

  Reference point  Accepted. The midpoint of EPA's own certification envelope,
                   851.75 kg/m3, is the centre of the API 32-37 range in
                   40 CFR 1065.703. Shifting it moves every state's deviation by
                   a constant and leaves the 38.3 kg/m3 spread unchanged.

  Cetane           Accepted. The direction is sign-robust in 4.7% of state-years
                   and is not asserted elsewhere. No cetane point estimate is
                   published; the reported quantity is a specification-derived
                   lower bound.

  Framing          Accepted. LIMITATIONS section 1 states that nobody sampled a
                   pump and that treating these values as measurements is misuse.

  Sector           Accepted, after revision. The prior wording said "many of the
                   engines CIDEX covers are nonroad" for a figure of 91.9%, and
                   sat at section 6 of 8. It is now section 1b, carries the
                   derived figure, and is repeated in the manuscript's own
                   statement of what it does not claim. The author agreed to this
                   revision before signing.

